.TH "GEN_BIND" "3const" "2026\-10\-09" "arena" "Arena Manuals"
.SH NAME
\fBGEN_BIND\fR \- get \fBC++\fR style in \fBC\fR.\&
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
There is special macro for better code.\& Example:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
/* You writing: */
ArenaAlloc(arena, sizeof(int));
/* With macro, you can write: */
arena->Alloc(sizeof(int));
/* Memory will be allocated in arena.\& */
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBBUT\fR you may bind arena only once.\& To setup and bind:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
/* Specify that we needs BIND function.\& */
#define \fBNEEDED_BIND\fR
#include "arena.h"

/* Generate BIND with ID '\&test\&' */
\fBGEN_BIND(\fItest\fB);\fR

/* Example: */
int main(void) {
  int* some_data = NULL;
  Arena* arena = InitArena(\fI4096\fR);
  /* Check for NULL.\&.\&.\& */

  /* BINDing to ID '\&test'\& arena \fIarena\fR.\& */
  \fBBindID\fItest\fB(arena);\fR

  /* Now, you can write so: */
  some_data = arena.\&Alloc(sizeof(int));
  /* Isn't ArenaAlloc(arena, sizeof(int)).\& */

  /* other code.\&.\&.\& */

  /* free arena and exit: */
  return 0;
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
You can rebind arena, but you can'\&t write \fIarena\fB.\&Alloc()\fR for it,
otherwise will be bug.\&
.PP
.SH RETURN VALUE
Return value is \fB0\fR or \fB1\fR if has error.\&
.PP
.SH AUTHORS
Project and man\-page: TheCRatTime
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBarena\fR(3), \fBInitArena\fR(3), \fBArenaAlloc\fR(3), \fBArenaFree\fR(3)
